  "notes": "Source: Fayetteville State University 2026-2027 'Bachelor of Science in Generic Nursing Freshman Curriculum Planning Guide and Four-Year Plan' (official, Office of the Registrar; last update 4/16/2026).\nTranscribed from the official Four-Year Plan tables (pages 6-7 of 7). The plan explicitly spans Year 1 Fall through Year 5 Spring (9 terms, including a Year 4 Summer term); some courses may be taken in an alternate order per the plan.\nCREDIBILITY FLAGS (catalog's own inconsistencies, transcribed as printed): (1) The plan grid sums to 132 credits, while the guide's program-requirements page states 'Total Credits 128'. (2) The grid lists 'NURS 360L' twice with different credits — 3 cr in Year 3 Spring and 2 cr in Year 4 Summer; the requirements page lists NURS 360L as 2 cr and separately requires NURS 350L (3 cr), which the grid never places — the Year 3 Spring row is most plausibly a typo for NURS 350L. It is recorded as a choice slot; confirm placement with an advisor. (3) The grid does not place NURS 326L (2 cr) or NURS 402 (3 cr), though both appear in the requirements list. (4) Minor grid typos corrected against the guide: 'SPEEC 200' -> SPEE 200 (guide: SPEE 200 or BADM 215); 'STATS 202' -> STAT 202.",
